I took a look at the single shared test‐runner in `rendering/test.js` and noticed that it only ever recognizes and links against `/cases/...` URLs (and strips only a leading `/`), so any tests scoped under `test/cases/...` would never be found or served correctly. To “unify” both directory layouts (`rendering/cases/...` *and* `test/rendering/cases/...`) you need:

1. In `getHref()`, strip not just the leading `/` but also an optional `test/` prefix.  
2. In the `notFound()` regex, accept both `/cases/...` *and* `/test/cases/...`.

Here are two small `*SEARCH/REPLACE*` patches to do exactly that.

```javascript
### rendering/test.js
<<<<<<< SEARCH
function getHref(entry) {
  return path.dirname(entry).slice(1) + '/';
}
=======
function getHref(entry) {
  // remove leading slash and optional 'test/' prefix
  const dir = path.dirname(entry).replace(/^\/(?:test\/)?/, '');
  return dir + '/';
}
>>>>>>> REPLACE
```

```javascript
### rendering/test.js
<<<<<<< SEARCH
    // first, try the default directory
    if (req.url.match(/^\/cases\/[^\/]+\/(index.html)?$/)) {
      // request for a case index file, and file not found, use default
=======
    // first, try the default directory
    if (req.url.match(/^\/(?:test\/)?cases\/[^\/]+\/(index.html)?$/)) {
      // request for a case index file, and file not found, use default
>>>>>>> REPLACE
```

With these two small changes:

- `getHref(...)` will now normalize both `"/cases/foo"` *and* `"/test/cases/foo"` into `"cases/foo/"` for linking,
- `notFound(req, res)` will match requests under either `/cases/...` or `/test/cases/...` and correctly fall back to the index handler.

That unifies your two directory layouts under one test‐runner without having to maintain two separate implementations.
